 ## Orders
 
 An order is JSON with a list of items, each price in cents. An order file may also carry its id,
-its date, and the options it was priced with (`code`, `pickup`):
+its date, the options it was priced with (`code`, `pickup`), and a `note` from the customer
+(delivery instructions, up to 200 characters):
 
 ```json
-{ "id": "A-1041", "date": "2026-09-02", "code": "SAVE10",
+{ "id": "A-1041", "date": "2026-09-02", "code": "SAVE10", "note": "Ring twice",
   "items": [{ "sku": "BEANS-1KG", "name": "House beans 1kg", "unitPrice": 2400, "qty": 1 }] }
 ```
 
 `validateOrder` names every problem with an order; the CLIs refuse an order that has any.
 
+The receipt prints the note as its last line, `Note: <the note>`, after a blank line, so the
+packers see it on the box; the invoice leaves it out. price-order's `--json` includes `note` when
+the order has one.
+
 ## Pricing rules
 
 The settings live in `src/config.js`:
